; Freshness lock (a co-truth lock for a *generated file*): the committed
; command reference must byte-match `yelu command-reference` output. So a
; command_names / family-list / command_kwargs change that isn't followed by a
; regenerate fails the build.
; Fix: `dune promote` (updates the committed markdown), or re-run
;   dune exec src/bin/yelu/yelu.exe -- command-reference
;
; Same pattern as test-tmgrammar. The point is that the reference can never
; lie: it is derived from the code (including Yc_cst_lower.family_of, the
; *actual* dispatch function, not a copy) and byte-compared on every test run.
; The hand-maintained table it replaces claimed "~60 of ~70 commands have a
; test" while 15 had none and 3 had no implementation at all.
(rule
 (target yc_command_reference.md.gen)
 (deps ../../src/bin/yelu/yelu.exe)
 (action
  (with-stdout-to yc_command_reference.md.gen
   (run ../../src/bin/yelu/yelu.exe command-reference --stdout))))

(rule
 (alias runtest)
 (action
  (diff ../../doc/lang/yc_command_reference.md yc_command_reference.md.gen)))
